		"b-20-implementation-roadmap-phase-deliverable-5": {
			"id": "b-20-implementation-roadmap-phase-deliverable-5",
			"type": "paragraph",
			"props": {},
			"text": [
				{
					"insert": "| Phase | Deliverable | Current Status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | Design doc and repo survey | Preserved in the markdown docs (the original HTML design artifact has been retired). |\n| 1 | Top-level orchestrator scaffold | Present under "
				},
				{
					"insert": "decomp-orchestrator/",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": ". |\n| 2 | Pi agent runtime bridge | Present for dry-run and live worker/review/curation agent sessions. |\n| 3 | State substrate | Present for runs, targets, epochs, target claims, worker states, checkpoints, events, cycles, and integrations. |\n| 4 | Read-only indexer | Present for "
				},
				{
					"insert": "report.json",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": " and "
				},
				{
					"insert": "objdiff.json",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": " fixture/live loading; richer graph edges are future work. |\n| 5 | Scheduler tick dry run | Present through deterministic "
				},
				{
					"insert": "tick",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": " and run-loop activation. |\n| 6 | Prompt builder and capability templates | Present under "
				},
				{
					"insert": "apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog/agents/{run,knowledge,pr}",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": " plus agent context manifest routes. |\n| 7 | One claimed worker | Present through target claims, worker state rows, and run-loop subprocess workers. |\n| 8 | Score integration dry run | Represented by "
				},
				{
					"insert": "regression-check",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": ", PR promotion reports, serial worker-output integration (apply-on-accept commits; an optional merge-on-finish mode existed earlier and was removed), conflict resolution, and boundary confirmation. |\n| 9 | Event-driven epoch admission loop | Present through "
				},
				{
					"insert": "run-loop",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": "; legacy scheduler aliases are removed. |\n| 9.5 | Managed process lifecycle | Present through direct "
				},
				{
					"insert": "run-loop",
					"attributes": {
						"code": true
					}
				},
				{
					"insert": " execution under the managed-process controller, with graceful signal settlement and no automatic restart. |\n| 10 | Fact-aware loop | Facts are represented in state, worker-state summaries, and checkpoint evidence; reducer/fact promotion is future work. |\n| 11 | Human dashboard | Present as the Bun/React UI for progress, work tables, process controls, collapsible rails, checkpointing, and PR handoff controls. |\n| 12 | Run summary artifact | Partially present through checkpoint artifacts, carry-forward ledgers, regression reports, PR split plans, and smoke summary artifacts. |"
				}
			],
			"children": []
		},
